{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273072-fera-breeding-ratios","id":1273072,"title":"Fera breeding ratios","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-06T04:23:21-08:00","id":1273072,"title":"Fera breeding ratios","content":"I'm trying to figure out the mating outcomes of different pairings in WtA. This is my understanding at the moment.<br /> <br /> Human + Human = 100% Human<br /> Human + Kinfolk = ~100% Human<br /> Human + Fera = ~100% Kinfolk<br /> Kinfolk + Kinfolk = 50% Kinfolk / 49% Human / 1% Fera<br /> Kinfolk + Fera = ~90% Kinfolk / ~10% Fera<br /> Fera + Fera = 100% Metis (If the breed can produce metis)<br /> <br /> Sources:<br /> [W20 Corebook p. 378]<br /> [Kinfolk Unsung Heroes p. 13]<br /> <br /> Skills that affect breeding:<br /> <br /> Brood Kenning skill (Mokole) - Observe a target for a day, and then roll Brood Kenning + Wits (can be Intelligence, Perception, or Wits as chosen by Storyteller). Difficulty is 9 but can be reduced by observing the target longer. Each success increases the chance of a Mokole offspring by 1%. [Breedbook Mokole p. 52]<br /> <br /> When a Fera and kinfolk mate, every dot of Pure Breed skill on the kinfolk increases the chance of producing a Fera child by 5%. This only works for Kinfolk. A Fera with Pure Breed doesn't increase the odds. When 2 kinfolk mate every dot of Pure Breed between them increases the chance of a Fera by 1%. [Kinfolk Unsung Heroes p. 51]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11840,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","user":"gx240","date":". 01-24-2019, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T11:19:02-08:00","id":1273119,"title":"","content":"The only case of Fera + Human = 100% kinfolk are the Rokea, and that's only with humans (sharks still have a chance to change even if they aren't kin)<br /> <br /> I don't know if there are any hard fast numbers for non kin but I think it's so much lower than kin it isn't really worth trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/918-geeklord1","name":"geeklord1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar918_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T15:16:11-08:00","id":1273157,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't realize that. Where do kinfolk come from, if you can't make them reliably by breeding Fera and humans? Is there some other way to make humans into kin (gifts or rituals)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T17:46:55-08:00","id":1273181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gx240</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273072-fera-breeding-ratios?p=1273157#post1273157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn't realize that. Where do kinfolk come from, if you can't make them reliably by breeding Fera and humans? Is there some other way to make humans into kin (gifts or rituals)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still Human + Fera, It's just not 100% certain it'll breed a kinfolk, not a human, and less then 0.1% chance <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> it'll be fera</span></span></span>(assuming do to the human vs kin + fera appears to be a difference factor of 10 across most fera types save rokea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T18:42:13-08:00","id":1273193,"title":"","content":"Ok that makes sense. Do you happen to know what book has these numbers? I found a few of the ratios on page 13 of the Kinfolk Unsung Heroes book, but I'm curious where the rest are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11840,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","user":"gx240","date":". 12-06-2018, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T09:17:08-08:00","id":1273273,"title":"","content":"The Rokea book is where humans only create kinfolk is in the tribe book. I don't believe there's a hard statistics on non kin producing Fera, it's just stated as rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/918-geeklord1","name":"geeklord1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar918_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T11:07:26-08:00","id":1273912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>geeklord1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273072-fera-breeding-ratios?p=1273273#post1273273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rokea book is where humans only create kinfolk is in the tribe book. I don't believe there's a hard statistics on non kin producing Fera, it's just stated as rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not sure where Prometheas is getting the 0.1% thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T12:49:06-08:00","id":1273933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 