le can reach 45% (10% base +25% Pure Breed +10% Brood Kenning). Although of course it would be really rare to find a kinfolk with 5 Pure Breed or roll 10 successes on 10 dice, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11840,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","user":"gx240","date":". 01-24-2019, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11840-gx240","name":"gx240","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T03:55:41-08:00","id":1282406,"title":"","content":"Iiirc, the chance of pure bred offspring of a kin/kin-pairing is also increased, but only by 1%, if I'm not mistaken. Still, the rating of both parents applies, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T05:24:31-08:00","id":1282413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273072-fera-breeding-ratios?p=1282327#post1282327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinfolk Unsung Heros states that each dot in Pure Breed on the Kin-side increases the chance of pure bred offspring by 5%.<br /> <br /> Corax seem to not breed at all, but procreate by a Rite...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i think the corax are limited to using speciic lineages..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T05:48:00-08:00","id":1282416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1273072-fera-breeding-ratios?p=1282413#post1282413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think the corax are limited to using speciic lineages..</div> </div> </div> </div>I never found a reference to that, when I looked a while back. It seemed to me, as if any person with a suitable persona would be a valid target of the Rite. It also seemed as if age wasn't a concern, so even very old or very young people could be suitable targets. Also, the Rite doesn't require the participation or agreement of the targeted person, which means that Corax kind of are fomori - for they are a forced merge of a pre-existing (human) being and a spiritual identity (that is in this case, specifically grown for the purpose of creating a Corax within a spirit egg).<br /> <br /> I wonder who often a Corax doens't vet his target sufficie